      "title": "Working",
      "description": "All vacancies - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen Working at UG Where does your interest lie? All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts All vacancies Clear filters Filters sluiten × Select a job type for additional filter options ↻ Reset All vacancies Academic positions Non-academic positions Function type ↻ Reset (Full) Professor PhD Docent Post-doc Researcher Assistant Professor Expertise ↻ Reset Administration & secretarial Education & research support Facilities Finance & controlling HR IT Management Project management Faculty ↻ Reset Vastgoed en Investeringsprojecten Center for Information Technology University Services Faculty of Law Faculty of Science and Engineering Faculty of Philosophy Faculty of Arts University of Groningen Library Faculty of Behavioural and Social Sciences Faculty of Economics and Business Faculty of Spatial Sciences University Services Department Preliminary education ↻ Reset PhD Master’s degree (university) Level ↻ Reset University of applied sciences Senior secondary vocational education University FTE 0 1 Location ↻ Reset Groningen Didn't find what you were looking for? Sign up for the job alerts and don't miss a single vacancy Sign up for job alerts Are you a student at the University of Groningen? Then check out our platform RUGconnect for vacancies! 26 academic non-academic vacancies Senior project manager research Are you a positive, result-driven senior scientist who thrives on managing and conducting research & development projects and bringing them to insightful & successful completion? Do you have a passion for advancing astronomical instrumentation? The NOVA Sub-mm Group at the University of Groningen is looking for a project manager research to advance the group’s research and development of sub-millimeter receiver technology for astronomy. You will be responsible for advancing the research, development and optimization of cryogenic receivers and their detectors. With a compact team of instrument scientists you will enable future groundbreaking astronomical research through the development of new high-sensitivity heterodyne technologies and state-of-the-art instrumentation. Why would you want this job? Impactful research and innovation : with a compact team of instrument scientists you develop high-precision astronomical instrumentation, shaping the future of sub-mm astronomy. Collaborative and international team : you work with top experts in a dynamic, interdisciplinary environment with extensive global collaborations. Faculty of Science and Engineering 1 FTE 19 September 2026 €5.932 - €7.573 > Post-doc Researcher Postdoc position in Contemplative Science A 1-year postdoc position (0.8 fte) in contemplative science is available at the Bernoulli Institute of the University of Groningen in the Netherlands. The position is situated in the cognitive modeling group and is funded by Marieke van Vugt’s Consciousness Foundation grant “Can reasoning dissolve the boundaries between self and others?”. In this project, we seek to investigate the neural correlates of the dissolution of boundaries between self and others. Faculty of Science and Engineering 0.8 FTE 30 September 2026 €4.251 - €4.599 > Docent Junior Lecturer in Innovation Management & Strategy The Innovation Management and Strategy (IM&S) department of the Faculty of Economics and Business (FEB), University of Groningen, The Netherlands, is looking for one Junior Lecturer (1.0 FTE). Faculty of Economics and Business 1 FTE 31 October 2026 €3.706 - €5.760 > PhD PhD in behavioural neurobiology We are looking for a PhD candidate to join our Neurobiology team. Faculty of Science and Engineering 1 FTE 15 September 2026 €3.204 - €4.051 > Docent Senior Lecturer in Economic evaluation in healthcare / Health Technology Assessment (HTA) The University of Groningen, Faculty of Economics and Business, is seeking a Senior Lecturer in Economic evaluation in healthcare / Health Technology Assessment (HTA) to join our team for course coordination and teaching in the MSc Business Administration Health program. Within our faculty, the successful candidate will take on the responsibility for the coordination, lecturing, examination, and thesis supervision in the field of economic evaluation methods and their application to managerial and clinical (including pharmaceutical) innovations in the health sector. Faculty of Economics and Business 0.2 FTE 15 September 2026 €6.764 - €8.199 > PhD PhD position Using microfluidics to observe and manipulate coacervate droplets We are looking for a 4-year PhD candidate to join our nationally funded, multi-partner research consortium, Towards De-Novo Life. The main aim of this interdisciplinary project is to achieve minimal life based on chemical rather than biological components such as DNA, proteins or other macromolecules. Our PhD candidate will contribute by developing new microfluidic tools to work with micrometer-sized coacervate droplets, the compartments in which chemical replication, growth and evolution will take place. Faculty of Science and Engineering 1 FTE 12 October 2026 €3.204 - €4.051 > Post-doc Researcher Postdoc position in Persuasion in Hybrid Intelligence Systems A 3-year postdoc position in artificial intelligence is available at the Bernoulli Institute of the University of Groningen in the Netherlands. The position is situated in the multi-agent systems group as part of the Hybrid Intelligence Centre, under the joint supervision of Dr. Harmen de Weerd, Prof.dr. Rineke Verbrugge, and Dr. Max van Duijn (Leiden University). Faculty of Science and Engineering 0.8 - 1 FTE 6 September 2026 €4.251 - €4.599 > Post-doc Researcher Postdoc position One Size Fits None: matching engagement to context Dutch national policy and legislation has high expectations of “bottom-up” provisioning systems for essential services, such as care and energy, where citizens take active roles in the set-up and functioning of an initiative. This requires local civil servants to engage citizens in policy design, implementation, and governance on a broad range of topics as established by, for example, the Climate Agreement, the Environment and Planning Act, and the Act to strengthen participation at the local level. While there is no shortage of public participation approaches policy makers can use to structure their citizen engagement interventions, systematic knowledge of which approach works best, when, where, and for whom is lacking. Hence, in their efforts to engage citizens, local civil servants run the risk of flying blind, lacking insight into which, if any, are the most adequate tools in their local context – for the specific community, specific problem at hand, at the given level of policymaking, and in the given social, economic, historical, and cultural conditions. The research you conduct in this postdoc project will help ameliorate this situation. Faculty of Behavioural and Social Sciences 18 September 2026 €3.706 - €5.760 > PhD PhD position Neuroscience Understanding how patterns of neural activity give rise to behavior is a central challenge in neuroscience. Most of what we know about this relationship comes from rodent experiments performed under tightly controlled laboratory conditions. While these approaches are essential for identifying neural mechanisms, they capture only a fraction of the behavioral repertoire animals display in more complex environments. Faculty of Science and Engineering 1 FTE 18 September 2026 €3.204 - €4.051 > Post-doc Researcher Postdoc position in detecting cognitive strategies in EEG data The ultimate objective of this project is to detect cognitive strategies in single-trial EEG data. In very broad terms, we will use the HMP method (https://github.com/GWeindel/hmp) to discover cognitive operations in existing data, label these operations, and then train transformer models to predict sequences of operations in unseen data. Please see Weindel, Borst, & van Maanen, eLife, 2025, Weindel, van Maanen, & Borst, Imaging Neuroscience, 2024, and Den Otter, Weindel, Stuit, Van Maanen, Plos Computational Biology, 2026 for more information about these methods. The goal of the project is to be able to track differences in strategy use between novices and experts on a task and map their learning trajectory. Faculty of Science and Engineering 0.8 - 1 FTE 15 September 2026 €4.251 - €4.599 > Frontoffice Medewerker Campus Binnenstad Werk jij graag met mensen en ben je daar ook goed in? Ben je gastvrij, vriendelijk en behulpzaam? Dan is deze functie echt wat voor jou! This vacancy is only available in Dutch University Services Department 7 September 2026 €3.147 - €3.622 > Post-doc Researcher Postdoctoral Researcher Urban Design and Inclusive Urban Mobility Join an ambitious, multidisciplinary project at the crossroads of interaction and urban design, where your research can shape the vision of open and accessible cities! This position is part of the NWO-funded research project BEAT (Building Equitable Accessibility Together) , which started in January 2026. Within the Faculty of Spatial Sciences, department of Spatial Planning we are looking for a postdoctoral researcher (0.8 – 1.0 FTE) on Inclusive mobility within BEAT NWO funded research project. Operating from the standpoint that mobility is essentially a subjective human experience, BEAT aims to investigate urban mobility barriers as they unfold in the daily activities of people. Rather than examining a specifi c mode of mobility (e.g., public transport, walking) or a single accessibility barrier, the focus of this project is the holistic experience of urban mobility in the daily lives of individuals with physical and cognitive diversities. The point of departure is “people”—their routines and travel behaviours, their daily frustrations with various mobility obstacles, and the impact of these hindrances on their personal, social, and professional lives. BEAT investigates a wide range of barriers that may be labelled as temporary or even mundane. Examples of such temporary-but-everyday barriers include construction sites and road works planned by municipalities, but also a variety of unplanned situations, such as improperly parked delivery vehicles, poorly placed planters and bikes on the sidewalk, unauthorised market stalls, and so forth. While each of these situations may be perceived as a temporary problem, collectively they form a permanent reality of how we experience our cities. These barriers signify an “informal” layer of inaccessibility superimposed on more structural or “formal” accessibility problems in the city. This informal layer is highly diverse, stems from many underlying causes and factors, and highlights a notable knowledge gap. Faculty of Spatial Sciences 0.8 - 1 FTE 20 September 2026 €3.706 - €5.760 > Post-doc Researcher Comparative Historical Analysis of Welfare Provision and Demographic Changes Within the Chair Group of Economic and Social History, Faculty of Arts at the University of Groningen, the Netherlands, a Postdoctoral Researcher position is currently available for the period of 2 years (24 months). The position will be within the ERC-funded project “Coping with decline: Comparative social-historical analysis of depopulation and community welfare in Europe, 1950-2022 (DEPOP)”: http://www.rug.nl/let/depop Faculty of Arts 0.8 FTE 20 September 2026 €3.706 - €5.760 > PhD PhD position in Neuromorphic Computing, FPGA Design, and Hardware Acceleration Are you excited about designing the next generation of energy-efficient AI hardware? Do you want to contribute to cutting-edge research at the intersection of neuromorphic computing, computer architecture, and hardware acceleration? The University of Groningen is seeking a highly motivated PhD candidate to join the international QuNeCo project, a collaborative research initiative between leading universities in the Netherlands and Japan. As part of an interdisciplinary team, you will develop novel neuromorphic computing architectures inspired by the human brain to enable future heterogeneous computing systems with unprecedented energy efficiency and performance. This PhD position offers the opportunity to collaborate with internationally renowned researchers, publish in leading conferences and journals, and gain experience in architecture design, hardware implementation, FPGA prototyping, and AI applications. Faculty of Science and Engineering 1 FTE 31 October 2026 €3.204 - €4.051 > PhD Three PhD positions in ML-guided directed evolution Are you passionate about combining the directed evolution of diverse biomolecules with deep learning approaches and contributing to the development of better (bio)catalysts and drugs? We are offering three fully-funded, 4-year PhD positions at the University of Groningen or the Technical University of Eindhoven. Faculty of Science and Engineering 1 FTE 15 October 2026 €3.204 - €4.051 > Assistant Professor Assistant professor in Digital Marketing Analytics / AI Within the Department of Marketing, Faculty of Economics and Business, University of Groningen, The Netherlands, a position is available for an assistant professor in Digital Marketing Analytics / AI. Faculty of Economics and Business 0.8 - 1 FTE 21 September 2026 €4.925 - €6.682 > Directeur School of Science and Engineering (0,8-1,0 fte) Wil jij richting geven aan het onderwijs van een van de grootste faculteiten van de Rijksuniversiteit Groningen? Heb je een duidelijke visie op universitair onderwijs én ervaring met leidinggeven in een complexe organisatie? Dan zijn wij op zoek naar jou. This vacancy is only available in Dutch Faculty of Science and Engineering 0.8 - 1 FTE 3 September 2026 €7.682 - €9.862 > Lid Dierexperimentencommissie Rijksuniversiteit Groningen (DEC-RUG) Wil jij bijdragen aan verantwoord en zorgvuldig dieronderzoek? En meedenken over de balans tussen wetenschappelijke vooruitgang en dierenwelzijn? De Dierexperimentencommissie van de Rijksuniversiteit Groningen (DEC-RUG) zoekt nieuwe externe leden. De DEC-RUG beoordeelt dierproeven binnen de RUG en het Universitair Medisch Centrum Groningen (UMCG). Daarbij staat één vraag centraal: wegen de mogelijke opbrengsten van het onderzoek op tegen de belasting voor het dier? Op basis van een zorgvuldige ethische en wetenschappelijke afweging adviseert de DEC de Centrale Commissie Dierproeven (CCD), die hierover een besluit neemt. This vacancy is only available in Dutch 10 September 2026 > Assistant Professor Universitair Docent Sociologie (Arbeid, Organisaties, Instituties) De Faculteit Gedrags- en Maatschappijwetenschappen van de Rijksuniversiteit is op zoek naar een Universitair Docent op het gebied van de Sociologie van Arbeid, Organisaties en Instituties. Deze positie is binnen de basiseenheid Sociologie. This vacancy is only available in Dutch Faculty of Behavioural and Social Sciences 0.8 FTE 10 September 2026 €4.925 - €7.573 > Post-doc Researcher Postdoctoral Researcher – Next-gen sequencing for machine-learning guided directed evolution Are you passionate about interfacing state-of-the-art sequencing techniques with deep learning approaches to accelerate the directed evolution of tailor-made (bio)catalysts and drugs? Supported by the Machine-Learning Guided Directed Evolution (ML-GUIDE) consortium, we are offering a fully funded Postdoctoral Researcher position at the University of Groningen. Faculty of Science and Engineering 15 September 2026 €4.251 - €5.760 > Technisch Specialist GBS – Applicatiebeheer & Engineering Ben jij de technische spil achter onze gebouwautomatisering omgeving? Heb jij een scherp analytisch oog voor complexe systemen en weet jij als geen ander de brug te slaan tussen operationele technologie en IT? Dan zoeken wij jou. This vacancy is only available in Dutch University Services 0.8 - 1 FTE €3.873 - €4.925 > PhD PhD position in Moral Philosophy, Conceptual Engineering, and Ethics of Emerging Technologies The Department of Ethics, Social and Political Philosophy at the University of Groningen is inviting applications for a fully-funded PhD position. Candidates are encouraged to submit their own research proposal that engages with questions in moral philosophy, conceptual engineering, and ethics of emerging technologies. Proposals may, for example, address themes such as conceptual ethics, meaningful human control, responsibility and control gaps, value-sensitive design, and the ethics of autonomous and AI-driven systems, as well as related questions. Faculty of Philosophy 1 FTE 13 September 2026 €3.204 - €4.051 > Senior Beheerder ICT - Microsoft Client platform Word jij enthousiast van moderne Microsoft-werkplekken die altijd beschikbaar, veilig en up-to-date moeten zijn in een omgeving waar technologie, onderwijs en onderzoek samenkomen? Bij het Centrum voor Informatie Technologie (CIT) van de Rijksuniversiteit Groningen (RUG) – één van de oudste en meest innovatieve universiteiten van Nederland – zoeken wij een Senior Beheerder ICT – Microsoft Client platform met technische diepgang, overzicht en een passie voor end-user computing. Als senior specialist speel jij een sleutelrol in het ontwerpen, beheren en doorontwikkelen van onze werkplekvoorzieningen voor duizenden studenten en medewerkers. Je krijgt ruimte om te verbeteren, te automatiseren en richting te geven, binnen een team waar hard wordt gewerkt én gelachen. Wil jij bijdragen aan betrouwbare en toekomstbestendige digitale werkplekken voor onderwijs en onderzoek? Kom ons Endpoint & Servermanagement team versterken! This vacancy is only available in Dutch Center for Information Technology 1 FTE €3.706 - €6.682 > Senior Windows Server Beheerder Bouw mee aan een veilige, stabiele en toekomstbestendige Microsoft-infrastructuur voor onderwijs en onderzoek. Word jij enthousiast van robuuste Windows Server-omgevingen, strakke Active Directory-structuren en security die klopt tot in de details? Wil je werken in een omgeving waar complexiteit, schaal en maatschappelijke impact samenkomen? Zoek jij technische diepgang, vrijheid, vertrouwen én een team waar hard gewerkt wordt maar ook gelachen? Dan pas je perfect bij ons. This vacancy is only available in Dutch Center for Information Technology 0.8 - 1 FTE €3.706 - €6.682 > Projectleider Installatietechniek Ben jij een doortastende organisator met een passie voor techniek en vastgoed? Krijg jij energie van het aansturen van complexe onderhouds- en bouwprojecten, waarin kwaliteit, samenwerking en resultaat centraal staan? Wil jij bijdragen aan toekomstbestendig vastgoed binnen een toonaangevende universiteit? Dan zoeken wij jou als projectleider Vastgoed bij de Rijksuniversiteit Groningen (RUG)! This vacancy is only available in Dutch Vastgoed en Investeringsprojecten 0.8 - 1 FTE €3.706 - €5.760 > Domeinarchitect Domeinen Bedrijfsvoering en Onderwijs Binnen de Rijksuniversiteit Groningen (RUG) zoeken we naar een enterprisearchitect, die in staat is om een visie op architectuur en informatievoorziening te formuleren en op strategisch niveau te adviseren. Een verantwoordelijke baan waarbij je je inzet voor de Domeinen Onderwijs en Organisatiesystemen. This vacancy is only available in Dutch Center for Information Technology 0.8 - 1 FTE €6.934 - €7.573 > < 1 2 3 > Senior project manager research Are you a positive, result-driven senior scientist who thrives on managing and conducting research & development projects and bringing them to insightful & successful completion? Do you have a passion for advancing astronomical instrumentation? The NOVA Sub-mm Group at the University of Groningen is looking for a project manager research to advance the group’s research and development of sub-millimeter receiver technology for astronomy. You will be responsible for advancing the research, development and optimization of cryogenic receivers and their detectors. With a compact team of instrument scientists you will enable future groundbreaking astronomical research through the developm